{
  "sourceId": "thinksr",
  "title": "ThinkSR: compact thought, dense output",
  "lang": "en",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s01-flow",
      "intent": "The recurrence returns to the DQ-CTM thought stage, while the dense carrier stays in the image pipeline.",
      "claim": "ThinkSR end to end: encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, decoder.",
      "narration": "The image first becomes features, then those features are partitioned into windows without leaving the dense carrier behind. The compact thought process reads and updates those windows through repeated ticks. The loop returns only to the thought stage, so the encoder and decoder are not rerun each tick. The same DQ-CTM parameters are reused across ticks. The close view isolates the repeated thought stage because that is where recurrence lives.",
