      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation first makes a dense feature field, then partitions that field into tokens without dropping the field.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into a dense feature field. The field is the carrier that stays spatial rather than becoming only a compact thought. The window operator partitions that field into tokens while keeping every token in the carrier equation.",
